#!/usr/bin/perl
# exp 0381: HANDOFF rows F660-F666 after the highest F row present, and notes on F443 and Q22.
use strict; use warnings;
my ($handoff) = @ARGV;
local $/;
open my $h, '<', $handoff or die; my $s = <$h>; close $h;
my $c;
$c = ($s =~ s/^\| F443 \| \*\*One S6N RT-on run/| F443 | *Refined by F663 (exp 0381): the 16:25 start-up fault of 10-29 is the same family with the same garbage high dword, made inside the shader; the IB's `USER_DATA_5` was 0x11 and the target mapped.* **One S6N RT-on run/m); die "F443 $c" unless $c == 1;
$c = ($s =~ s/^\| Q22 \| \*\(2026-10-24\)\* \*\*Stray TCP writes outside guest memory\.\*\*/| Q22 | *(2026-10-24)* *Narrowed by F663 (exp 0381): the junk-high-dword faults of F443 and 10-29 16:25 come from one compute family (`USER_DATA_3\/4` offsets under `USER_DATA_5` = 0x11; at 16:25 the BVH adjacency build 0x909977100) whose shader forms a garbage high dword; which load is open.* **Stray TCP writes outside guest memory.**/m); die "Q22 $c" unless $c == 1;
my $rows = <<'R';
| F660 | **The 18:08:13 hang (10-29, shared normal 58c4a627, RT on) is a static graphics-pipe stall unlike every healthy sample and unlike F403 and F519.** Its devcoredump reads `GRBM_STATUS` 0xa2712028 (GE, PA, SX, SPI busy; SC, DB, CB, TA idle), SE0/SE1 0x0d000004, `GRBM_STATUS2` 0x50000008 (no TCP, EA, `EA_LINK`, UTCL2), `CP_STALLED_STAT2` 0x218000, `CP_BUSY_STAT` 0x448400; the five sampler records over 1.2 s are identical. Against exp 0378's 40 healthy forced samples the nearest differs by 18 status bits (F534's F403 sample: 1 bit); no healthy sample has GE busy and TA idle with the partial-flush and EOP waits (0/40; the three with GE busy and the partial-flush wait have TA, EA and `EA_LINK_BUSY` busy). Waves resident, no memory traffic, the geometry front end holding work. (F588 on exp 0380's branch named the state; this is its comparison.) | experiment 0381 (`ana0381.py`, `raw/ana.txt`; Linux v7.2 `gc_10_1_0_sh_mask.h`) | High for the state |
| F661 | **One sample tells the three stall classes apart on the records so far: F535's rule (partial-flush wait, `EA_LINK_BUSY` clear) plus GE busy, TA idle and the EOPD wait marks the graphics stall (18:08 yes, F403 no, healthy 0/40); F589's compute terms mark F403 (F403 yes, 18:08 no, healthy 0/40); F519's ASTRO BOT stop has no partial-flush wait and fires neither.** An early warning should log `gfx-stall-early` and `f403-early` separately and leave F519's class to the stall clock. Design only. | experiment 0381 (`raw/ana.txt`) | Medium: one graphics event, 40 healthy samples |
| F662 | **18:08's stuck dcb #127530 ends with one fast-launch NGG point-list pass (`VGT_SHADER_STAGES_EN` 0x482030: ES_EN 2, GS_EN, PRIMGEN_EN, GS_FAST_LAUNCH 1; ES programs 0x11d00f85xx–0x11d01345xx; no HS or LS anywhere in the probe's tracked state, so not tessellation), and at the timeout 13 of its 15 `DRAW_INDIRECT` argument slots (`SET_BASE` 1 0x1193ad3900 + 0xc4a0…0x229a0) hold ascending 16-bit pairs (000f0101 000f0102 …, 00050006 00050007 …, 000a01a7 000a01a8 …), i.e. 2^16–2^20 vertices times as many instances; two are sane (0x35×1, 1×1).** A fast-launch draw with such counts launches 10^10–10^12 threads, which fits the static GE/PA/SX/SPI-busy state: the graphics twin of F403 sub-class B's index-like dims (F590). Open: whether the CP fetched these words or the title overwrote the slots after a sane fetch (the CPU view is read ~2 s later; at 12:12 it was the reverse, F553). Candidate hanging draw: dword 12640, the first such slot. | experiment 0381 (`raw/hang-1808-indirect-draws.txt`; the probe dump `play-20261029-1716/gc/ib-timeout-00127530-dcb-14945.bin` and its journal private) | Medium: one event, CPU view at the timeout |
| F663 | **The 16:25 start-up fault (10-29, exp 0380 start 1) is F443's class exactly: the IB carried the right pointers and the shader made the garbage high dword.** 887 of the dcb's 893 dispatches set `COMPUTE_USER_DATA_5` = 0x11 with `USER_DATA_3/4` 0x8c64e600–0x8ce71c00; every fault page has one of these low dwords under 0x860 (0x8608c65c000 = `USER_DATA_3` 0x8c65c000 of five dispatches; devcd1's 0x8608c728000), as F443's had under 0xe380 (F467). The intended 0x118c65xxxx–0x118c728000 lie in the learned window 0x118a000000 + 96 MiB (list a7cc8581), so neither a lazy view (F468) nor the host's user-data tracking explains it; no real-address fault came first. Which load gives the high half (the `LOAD_SH_REG_INDEX` table at 0x909842dc0, the compacted list, a descriptor) needs 0x909977100's code. | experiment 0381 (`raw/hang-1625-dispatch-pointers.txt`, `raw/hang-1625-devcd-regs.txt`; dumps private) | High for the pointers; the source of the high dword open |
| F664 | **The lost picture after 16:25's successful resets is the killed job's label writes: the next job waits on a 64-bit label (devcd2 16:25:44: shaders idle, the ME's newest header `WAIT_REG_MEM64` 0xc0079300, `CP_STALLED_STAT2` 0x10000) that dcb #32979 (45 label writes, e.g. 0x12004bac80 to be 2, read 1 at the timeout) never wrote.** F403's devcd4 pattern. Recovery candidate (TODO(verify) against the title's expectations): after a reset that succeeds, the host writes the killed job's remaining label values, which its filter knows. | experiment 0381 (`raw/hang-1625-devcd-regs.txt`) | High for the wait; the candidate untested |
| F665 | **16:25 ties to the BVH work through the program only: 0x909977100 is the adjacency build, a consumer of the compaction 0x909974400's compacted list (exp 0160's reading), and the compaction runs in the shared launchers (`BC5_DIRECT_SKIP_PGM=0`, exp 0378 B1).** F207's night-scene fault is the geometry engine reading page 0 under the full-state prefix, another client and mechanism. FORCE_START is not needed either: F443 happened without it. | experiment 0381 (README §1, §3); exp 0160 hand-over note | Medium |
| F666 | **Next, cheapest first: (1) a box read of the `op 24`/`op 2c` probe lines of the earlier hangs' journals (09:48, 12:12, 14:04; 10-28 18:15, 23:36) as the control for F662's CPU view; (2) a host-only submit-time journal of `DRAW_INDIRECT` arguments in the 0x1193… window with counts above 2^16 flagged (no packet); (3) a fix candidate, default off: a CP-side draw guard (`COND_WRITE`/`COND_EXEC` on vertex and instance counts, skip above a limit), the draw analogue of the dispatch check, with F590's caveat; (4) for 16:25, 0x909977100's code for the high half, and F664's label-completion recovery.** | experiment 0381 (Verdict) | Plan |
R
my @f = ($s =~ /^\| F(\d+) \|/mg); my $max = (sort { $b <=> $a } @f)[0];
$c = ($s =~ s/(^\| F$max \|[^\n]*\n)/$1$rows/m); die "F$max $c" unless $c == 1;
open $h, '>', $handoff or die; print $h $s; close $h;
print "rows after F$max\n";
